    "final_message": "I built the Everbloom app in SwiftUI in the project root. Every item on the spec's Done checklist passed on the iOS Simulator using the Release build, except that a variant switch never changed the price (see below). The only thing I couldn't verify is the physical device: the device build compiles unsigned (`CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO`), but I never had a device to install or launch it on.\n\n**What was checked**\n- **Builds:** the device and Simulator commands in `BUILD.md` both succeed from a clean state. The device app is 2.0 MB, arm64 only.\n- **Flows:** an XCUITest target I added drove each flow:\n  - Home loads.\n  - The \"Urban Transit Essentials\" collection scrolls to its last product (84 of 84), and each of the four sorts reloads it.\n  - Searching \"shirt\" scrolls through all 67 results and opens a product.\n  - Picking an option switches the selected variant, and a recommendation opens another product.\n  - Add to cart switches to the Cart tab and shows the badge. The stepper changes the quantity and subtotal; going to 0 shows the empty state.\n  - Check out opens the checkout page in the in-app browser.\n- **Price on variant switch:** no product in the top 100 has variants at different prices, so the price never actually changes on this catalog.\n- **Error state:** with the endpoint down, Home shows \"Couldn't load products\". Once a local proxy came up, Retry loaded Home.\n- **Log marker:** `SHOPBENCH home_ready` appears once per launch (two launches, two lines).\n- **Identifiers:** XCUITest found every accessibility identifier in the spec's table.\n- **Endpoint override:** `SHOP_API_URL` works; the tests ran against a local proxy through it.\n\n**Things you might trip over**\n- **Port 8787 is taken on this Mac.** Another Python process (PID 77646, not mine) is listening there, so I used port 8799 for my proxy and left that process alone.\n- **Local Network prompt.** iOS asks once for Local Network permission the first time the app contacts a LAN address like the replay server. It may need to be accepted on the test iPhone before benchmarking.\n- **No edge-swipe back.** I drew the design's own headers in place of the system navigation bar, which disables swipe-back; the back buttons work.\n- **Tab bar is hand-built.** It's made from SwiftUI views rather than the system `TabView`, so it can match the design and carry the `tab-*` and `cart-badge` identifiers.\n\n**Choices recorded in `NOTES.md`**\n- I left out the design's \"See all\" link because the spec doesn't list it.\n- The empty cart keeps the design's \"Start shopping\" button, which switches to Home.\n- If a cart request fails on the network, the app shows an alert.\n\nThere are no third-party dependencies. The Xcode project is checked in, so building needs only Xcode 27.2. XcodeGen is needed only if you edit `project.yml`.\n\nFiles are in the project root:\n- `BUILD.md`\n- `NOTES.md`\n- `project.yml`\n- `Everbloom.xcodeproj`\n- `Everbloom/`\n- `EverbloomUITests/`"
